'auth_gate|VERIFY'; echo \"armB_rc=${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"; rm -f /tmp/node-status.json; rm -rf \"$d\""}
 {"id":"CF-153","title":"P3 \u2014 the create path cannot honour the remedy its own error prints: node-create.sh has no --ref flag, so a repo whose default branch is not 'main' can never be created by README step 3","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":2,"created_at":"2026-11-04T02:55:17Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T02:55:17Z","detail":{"evidence":[{"run_id":"code-factory-dogfood-2026-11-04-02-39-16","ts":"2026-11-04T03:20:00Z","artifacts":["docs/audits/code-factory-dogfood-2026-11-04-02-39-16.md"]}]},"reasoning":"Dogfood walk 2026-11-04 (tick code-factory-dogfood-2026-11-04-02-39-16) at the published tip c29c024, under the family barrier (sibling lane code-factory status=running), from a throwaway clone: `git diff --name-only f26a608 c29c024 -- scripts/ README.md` = 0 files, so the arms hold at both tips.\n\nARM A (the control-host create path), verbatim:\n  $ BUNKER_SERVER=no-such-server bash scripts/node-create.sh --project p --repo https://github.com/git/git --harness hermes --ref master\n  unknown arg: --ref\n  rc=2\n\nARM B (the node-side entry point, layer 40 only, fresh HOME):\n  $ HOME=$(mktemp -d) bash scripts/project-node.sh --apply --layers 40 --project refproof --repo https://github.com/git/git\n  [40] repo\n    ..    cloning https://github.com/git/git @ main\n    FAIL  repo_clone \u2014 ref 'main' was not found; pass --ref <branch-or-tag>\n  NODE: FAIL (1)\n\nThe node's failure text names `--ref` as the remedy; the only documented control-host command that creates a node rejects that exact flag, and does not say which command accepts it. Mechanism, from the tree: scripts/project-node.sh:33 `REF=\"${NODE_REF:-main}\"` and :53 `--ref) REF=\"$2\"` (the node side supports the selection); scripts/node-create.sh:56-67 parses --project/--repo/--harness/--agent/--ttl/--port/--staged-files only, so --ref falls to the `*)` arm at :65; :103 forwards exactly NODE_PROJECT and NODE_GATEWAY_PORT into the node's `bash -lc` and passes --project/--harness/--repo, never a ref, so NODE_REF cannot cross either and there is no second route. README.md:80-81 states \"`--ref` defaults to `main`, so a public repo whose default branch is named differently needs `--ref <branch>`\". Consequence: a repo whose default branch is not main (git.git, linux, a large share of GitHub) cannot be turned into a node by README step 3, and the operator's only feedback is a rejection of the flag the previous error told them to use.\n\nNot a duplicate, checked row by row on the c29c024 board: CF-034 (complete) is --ref on project-node.sh plus clone-failure wording, not the control-host create path having no flag; CF-126 (pending) is CRIER_URL not handed to the node \u2014 same control\u2192node handoff family, different variable, different layer (00 vs 40), different remedy; CF-125 (pending) is --harness typo vs unmeasured adapter; CF-041 (complete) is Quick start env-ordering and a nonexistent --agent.","acceptance_criteria":"0. Reproduce on the current tree from the repo root: the probe below prints `unknown arg: --ref` with arm_create_rc=2 and prints `FAIL  repo_clone \u2014 ref 'main' was not found; pass --ref <branch-or-tag>` in the layer-40 arm, and leaves no agent behind (BUNKER_SERVER is deliberately a nonexistent server).\n1. scripts/node-create.sh accepts a ref selection \u2014 a `--ref <branch-or-tag>` flag, or documented NODE_REF forwarding \u2014 and passes it through to the node's `project-node.sh --ref`, so a node created for a public repo whose default branch is not `main` reaches `PASS  repo_clone` naming the branch it cloned instead of `ref 'main' was not found`.\n2. The self-contradiction is closed in the same commit, one of two ways, and the commit message says which: the flag exists and README.md:80-81's advice is reachable from step 3, or README.md:80-81 stops offering `--ref` as the create-path remedy and names the command that does take it.\n3. Negative control: on the pre-fix tree the probe's two arms disagree exactly as recorded here (a command tells the operator to pass a flag; the command the operator is told to run rejects it). The new gate arm must fail on that tree.\n4. `bash scripts/node-create.sh --staged-files` stays at its shipped five-file set and rc=0 (the ref must not change the staged set), and a failed create still prints the explicit-server destroy command naming the agent it spawned.\n5. `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS` at the fixed tip with the new arm visible as a named PASS row (AGENTS.md rule 2), and `bash scripts/boardctl validate` prints `RESULT: OK`.","probe":"cd \"$(git rev-parse --show-toplevel)\" || exit 99; echo ARM_create_path:; BUNKER_SERVER=no-such-server bash scripts/node-create.sh --project p --repo https://github.com/git/git --harness hermes --ref master 2>&1 | head -2; echo \"arm_create_rc=${PIPESTATUS[0]}\"; echo ARM_node_layer40:; H=$(mktemp -d); HOME=\"$H\" bash scripts/project-node.sh --apply --layers 40 --project p --repo https://github.com/git/git 2>&1 | tail -3; rm -rf \"$H\"; echo \"pre-fix: 'unknown arg: --ref' (rc=2) + \\\"ref 'main' was not found; pass --ref <branch-or-tag>\\\"\""}
 {"id":"CF-154","title":"P4 \u2014 docs/BOARD.md's census block quotes a warning count that is not a function of the tree: two boardctl binaries print 55 vs 3 warnings for identical board bytes, and the '44 probe rows' class is gone from the current one","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":3,"created_at":"2026-11-04T03:01:29Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T03:01:33Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"f31a32fd16ac90aef2cb5907312ea9cf00bc21ea8a29fd8eea06496739b1ea6d"},"reasoning":"Measured by the docs lane tick code-factory-docs-2026-11-04-02-39-16 on 2026-11-04, in the canonical checkout.\n\ndocs/BOARD.md:76-79 (section \"Current measured state\") states: \"At this tree: 116 task rows, 168 events. `scripts/boardctl validate` prints `RESULT: OK (47 warning(s))` \u2014 44 rows carrying a free-form `probe` key, CF-034's free-form `guard_result`/`ci_result` prose, and the headerless board (no `board.jsonl`), so header-counter checks are skipped.\"\n\nTwo independent defects in that one paragraph.\n\n(1) The counts are stale: at 472e369 the same commands give 127 task rows / 193 events (11 rows and 25 events more than the block claims) \u2014 expected drift for a block that moves with every folded row, and owned by the sync-lane census work (CF-121/CF-122).\n\n(2) The warning count is instrument-dependent, which the block does not say and cannot express. ~/.local/bin/boardctl was replaced mid-tick (mtime 2026-11-03 21:56:15 -05:00, `boardctl version` -> `dev`, no version string available). Measured, same c29c024 board bytes, two binaries:\n  - old binary: `scripts/boardctl validate` -> `RESULT: OK (55 warning(s))`, warning rows naming `key(s) {probe} outside the declared canon` for each affected task;\n  - current binary: same bytes -> `RESULT: OK (3 warning(s))`, and `grep -ci probe` on the output returns 0, although `jq -c 'select(has(\"probe\"))' .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl | wc -l` returns 53 at 472e369 (52 at c29c024).\nSo the block's explanation \"44 rows carrying a free-form `probe` key\" names a warning class the current instrument cannot emit, and every warning count already printed into docs/audits/* (47, 46, 45, 55, 3 across this week) is unreproducible without also naming the binary that produced it.\n\nThis is the doc-lane reading of the same defect class as CF-081 (hand-typed counts) and CF-121 (tautological snapshot legs): there a count was stale, here the count is not even a function of the tree alone. Filed rather than fixed because the block belongs to the sync-lane census reconciliation and a second writer would collide.","acceptance_criteria":"1. Every warning count this repository's docs quote for `boardctl validate` is accompanied by the identity of the binary that printed it (`sha256sum \"$(command -v boardctl)\"`, plus its mtime), or the count is removed from the doc in favour of the command alone.\n2. Re-runnable proof of the defect, recorded in the row's evidence artifact: one board copy, two `boardctl` binaries, two different warning totals on identical bytes (`55` vs `3` measured on 2026-11-04), with `jq 'select(has(\"probe\"))' | wc -l` showing the free-form `probe` rows still present in both runs.\n3. docs/BOARD.md's \"Current measured state\" block no longer contains the sentence \"44 rows carrying a free-form `probe` key\" unless the binary it was measured with emits that warning class \u2014 the sentence is either re-derived from the current instrument's output or deleted.\n4. `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS` (exit 0) at the fixed tip, and the block's own command list still reproduces byte-for-byte what the doc states about rows and events.","probe":null,"foreman_note":"Evidence artifact: docs/audits/code-factory-docs-2026-11-04-CF-129.md section 5 carries the measured matrix (same c29c024 board bytes; old binary 55 warnings with probe-canon rows, current binary 3 warnings and grep -ci probe = 0; 53 rows still carry probe at 472e369) plus the binary mtime 2026-11-03 21:56:15 -05:00 and 'boardctl version -> dev'."}
+{"id":"CF-155","title":"P4 \u2014 docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md still states 29 selftest sections while tests/selftest.sh has 30: \u00a730 landed at 1b4b0b6 and the row's own shipped drift probe exits 1 at HEAD","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":1,"created_at":"2026-11-04T03:02:01Z","updated_at":"2026-11-04T03:02:01Z","detail":{"evidence":[]},"reasoning":"Measured at code-factory@c29c024 (re-verified at gh/main da84b0c). docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md states 29 numbered selftest sections twice (:7 '29 sections \u2014 plus two lettered sub-arms', :61 '`d02916e`, `tests/selftest.sh` has 29 numbered sections plus two lettered sub-arms (\u00a74b, \u00a77b)') and its reverse-direction table stops at \u00a729 (:69-96 \u2014 no \u00a730 row). tests/selftest.sh has 30: `say \"30. README Status rows 1 and 3 cite the interpreter-qualified --check\"` landed at 1b4b0b6 (2026-11-03 21:35:05, 'Addresses CF-093'), and the later c9848d7 ('docs(sync): reconcile the board census and the ACCEPTANCE-PLAN snapshot at 2c48149') re-anchored the row/event deltas while leaving the section count and the \u00a729-terminated table untouched. The instrument CF-099 shipped for exactly this drift (docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh) therefore exits 1 at HEAD with 'DRIFT: plan says 29 sections, tests/selftest.sh has 30'. Nothing forces a new numbered section to update the plan: no selftest arm reads docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md, so the gate stays green (SELFTEST: PASS at c29c024) while the plan describes a tree that no longer exists. DISTINCT FROM CF-113 (the census regex cannot see LETTERED sub-arms, \u00a77b) and CF-121 (the probe's snapshot leg is a tautology) and CF-115 (legs the probe certifies without measuring): this is a NUMBERED section the census sees, dropped by the plan side, and the probe's own measured leg is what reds. CF-099 is complete and was correct at its own closure commit a9d0cc8; the rot arrived later with 1b4b0b6, so this is fresh drift, not a reopen. ch:trace row=CF-154 spec=docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md wave=none:qa-tick-no-manifest test=tests/selftest.sh doc=docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md prompt=prompts/docs.md evidence=~/.hermes/stand-in/pm/code-factory-docs/docs-qa-2026-11-03-evidence.md witness=cmd:probe-153 verdict=none:filed-not-judged commit=none:not-yet-fixed memory=done:duckbrain-6a265050","acceptance_criteria":"0. Reproduce on the current tree from the repo root: the probe below prints `30`, then the two ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md lines that say `29` (`:7` and `:61`), then `DRIFT: plan says 29 sections, tests/selftest.sh has 30`, then `probe_rc=1`.\n1. `bash docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh` exits 0 at the fix commit and its `measured:` line reports `sections=30`.\n2. The section count stated in docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md equals `grep -cE '^say \"[0-9]+\\.' tests/selftest.sh`, and the reverse-direction table carries a row for `\u00a730` naming what governs it (README Status rows 1 and 3, board CF-093) beside the existing \u00a71-\u00a729 rows.\n3. A gate can fail on this drift: adding a numbered `say \"NN. ...\"` section without updating docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md makes `bash tests/selftest.sh` (or the committed probe wired into it) exit non-zero, and removing that section makes it pass again (the red-proof arm is named in the output, never the substring FAIL alone).\n4. `bash tests/selftest.sh` prints `SELFTEST: PASS` and `bash scripts/boardctl validate` prints `RESULT: OK` at the fix commit.","probe":"grep -cE '^say \"[0-9]+\\.' tests/selftest.sh; grep -n 'sections \u2014 plus two lettered' docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md; grep -n 'has 29 numbered sections' docs/ACCEPTANCE-PLAN.md; bash docs/audits/cf099-prd-drift-probe.sh; echo \"probe_rc=$?\""}
